# ---- Personal data (kept outside the repo, blocked here as a second layer) ----
data/
cache/
exports/
thumbs/
quarantine/

# `records/` used to be here, unanchored, and a gitignore pattern with
# no slash matches a directory of that name **at any depth**. It
# silently swallowed `packages/kiseki-core/src/kiseki/adapters/records/`
# -- the whole point of the pull request that added it -- and every
# test passed locally because the file was on disk. A fresh clone would
# have failed to import. Anchored to where a producer actually writes,
# and `tests/unit/test_the_source_is_all_here.py` now checks that no
# source file is ignored.
/records/
kiseki-data/records/
*.heic
*.HEIC
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.JPG
*.JPEG
*.png
*.mov
*.MOV
*.mp4
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

